#import std.logger;

error Failure { Failed; }

// Everything an `if` condition can say, in one entry.
//
//   * a **constant binding** read from inside a condition — `mask` below;
//   * the three **bitwise** operators `|`, `^` and `&`;
//   * the **connectives** `&&` and `||`;
//   * unary **`!`**.
//
// None of these is an operation the checker learned. Each is a token-tier
// construct that lowers onto the one branch primitive: `A || B` becomes the
// right-nested `if (A) { … } else if (B) { … }` a reader would have written by
// hand, and `!C` becomes an arm swap. Short-circuit is therefore *structural* —
// the second operand of a `||` is the condition of a branch sitting inside the
// first one's `else` arm, so the emitted C reaches it on exactly one path. The
// emitted C is byte-identical to the hand-written twin's; nothing downstream can
// tell a connective or a `!` was written.
//
// **The parentheses around each bitwise operand are load-bearing.** C ranks `|`,
// `^` and `&` *looser* than the comparisons, so C would read `mask | 3 == 15` as
// `mask | (3 == 15)`. This tier ranks them tighter, and rather than silently
// redefine a precedence every C programmer already carries, it requires the
// grouping: the ungrouped spelling is refused. Write the parentheses and the two
// languages agree about what you meant.
//
// The custody join is unmoved by any of this. Every level runs the same join, so
// all three arms below must still agree — which is why all three release.
//
// Walking the conditions with `mask = 12` (binary 1100):
//
//   `(mask | 3) == 14`      1100 | 0011 = 1111 = 15, so **false**, and the `&&`
//                           never reaches its right-hand side;
//   `!((mask ^ 5) == 9)`    1100 ^ 0101 = 1001 = 9, so the comparison is true
//                           and the `!` makes it **false** — the `||` therefore
//                           falls through to its right-hand side;
//   `(mask & 8) == 8`       1100 & 1000 = 1000 = 8, so **true**, and the second
//                           arm is the one that runs.
fn main() -> i32 {
    log_level trace;
    let mask = 12;
    let a = qcore_acquire(1, true, Failure);
    if ((mask | 3) == 14 && (mask & 4) == 4) {
        drop a;
    } else if (!((mask ^ 5) == 9) || (mask & 8) == 8) {
        drop a;
    } else {
        drop a;
    }
    return 0;
}
